{"from":"2:1","body":"<p><ref to=\"HAB.2.1\">1</ref> Unto Habakkuk, waiting for an answer, is shewn that he must wait by faith.<br/><ref to=\"HAB.2.5\">5</ref> The judgment upon the Chaldean for unsatiableness,<br/><ref to=\"HAB.2.9\">9</ref> for covetousness,<br/><ref to=\"HAB.2.12\">12</ref> for cruelty,<br/><ref to=\"HAB.2.15\">15</ref> for drunkenness,<br/><ref to=\"HAB.2.18\">18</ref> and for idolatry.<br/><br/><br/>stand.<br/><ref to=\"PSA.73.16 PSA.73.17 ISA.21.8 ISA.21.11 ISA.21.12\">Ps 73:16,17; Isa 21:8,11,12</ref><br/>tower. Heb. fenced place.<br/><ref to=\"2SA.18.24 2KI.9.17 2KI.17.9 ISA.21.5 ISA.62.6\">2Sa 18:24; 2Ki 9:17; 17:9; Isa 21:5; 62:6</ref><br/>and will.<br/><ref to=\"HAB.1.12-HAB.1.17 PSA.85.8\">1:12-17; Ps 85:8</ref><br/>unto me. or, in me.<br/><ref to=\"2CO.13.3 GAL.1.16\">2Co 13:3; Ga 1:16</ref><br/>when I am reproved. or, when I am argued with. Heb. upon myreproof, or arguing.<br/><ref to=\"JOB.23.5-JOB.23.7 JOB.31.35 JOB.31.37 JER.12.1\">Job 23:5-7; 31:35,37; Jer 12:1</ref></p>"}
